# Native-symbol allowlist for goldenflow. One symbol per line; `# reason` inline.
# A host reference whose symbol the static scanner can't attribute to a build
# (cross-kernel, or a deliberately-aspirational fallback with a tracked issue).
# EMPTY at bootstrap — the computed FAIL set is empty.
from_arrow  # Column::from_arrow is a #[pymethods] method, not a wrap_pyfunction! module export, so the scanner's registration parser structurally cannot see it. Referenced from engine/columnar.py's _CAPABILITIES table. The real fix is teaching check_native_symbols.py to parse #[pymethods] impl blocks; until then this entry stops a REAL symbol reading as a missing one.
